Stop process-lock checks from killing a single-process browser.

On a phone, opening an extension's page took the whole app down:
"Terminating renderer for bad IPC message, reason 1"
(RFH_CAN_COMMIT_URL_BLOCKED), then SIGTRAP on CrBrowserMain, from
ValidateURLAndOrigin via ValidateDidCommitParams.

A phone runs Chromium single-process, because the platform lets an app
start no other process. The browser, every page, every WebUI and every
extension share that one process, so a process lock or a grant can only
describe what the browser itself may commit -- which is everything. The
checks were refusing a chrome-extension:// page anyway, and a refusal
there is a "bad message", which in single-process mode is a deliberate
crash. Upstream already makes the same exception for WebUI in
CanRequestURL.

So on OHOS in single-process mode:

- CanCommitURL and CanAccessMaybeOpaqueOrigin allow what they would
  otherwise refuse. The second is also what an extension's service
  worker and storage are checked against, which may be why a service
  worker would not start ("No SW").
- A refused commit is logged with its URL, origin and lock in a release
  build, where the log said nothing about which URL it was.
- A bad message from the in-process renderer is refused and logged
  rather than crashing the app with every tab in it.

Tablets and 2in1s run renderers in processes of their own and none of
this applies to them.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after chromium-154-harmonyos.patch.

diff --git a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_frame_host_impl.cc b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_frame_host_impl.cc
--- a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_frame_host_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_frame_host_impl.cc
@@ -16199,6 +16199,13 @@ bool RenderFrameHostImpl::ValidateURLAndOrigin(
       // The origin and URL are safe to commit.
       break;
     case CanCommitStatus::CANNOT_COMMIT_URL:
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_OHOS)
+      // Said in a release build too: on a phone this is what took the whole
+      // browser down, and the log had no word on which URL.
+      LOG(ERROR) << "OHOS CANNOT_COMMIT_URL url '" << url << "' origin '"
+                 << origin << "' lock '" << process->GetProcessLock().ToString()
+                 << "'";
+#endif
       DLOG(ERROR) << "CANNOT_COMMIT_URL url '" << url << "'"
                   << " origin '" << origin << "'"
                   << " lock '" << process->GetProcessLock().ToString() << "'";
@@ -16211,6 +16218,11 @@ bool RenderFrameHostImpl::ValidateURLAndOrigin(
                                       bad_message::RFH_CAN_COMMIT_URL_BLOCKED);
       return false;
     case CanCommitStatus::CANNOT_COMMIT_ORIGIN:
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_OHOS)
+      LOG(ERROR) << "OHOS CANNOT_COMMIT_ORIGIN url '" << url << "' origin '"
+                 << origin << "' lock '" << process->GetProcessLock().ToString()
+                 << "'";
+#endif
       DLOG(ERROR) << "CANNOT_COMMIT_ORIGIN url '" << url << "'"
                   << " origin '" << origin << "'"
                   << " lock '" << process->GetProcessLock().ToString() << "'";
diff --git a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_process_host_impl.cc b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_process_host_impl.cc
--- a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_process_host_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_process_host_impl.cc
@@ -3331,9 +3331,19 @@ void RenderProcessHostImpl::ShutdownForBadMessage(
   }
 
   if (run_renderer_in_process()) {
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_OHOS)
+    // On a phone single-process is not a debugging mode but the only one
+    // there is, and the process "killed" here is the whole app: every tab,
+    // and the shell with it. The message is refused -- the caller has
+    // already rejected it -- and the browser carries on.
+    LOG(ERROR) << "OHOS: bad message from the in-process renderer, ignored "
+                  "rather than crashing the browser";
+    return;
+#else
     // In single process mode it is better if we don't suicide but just
     // crash.
     NOTREACHED();
+#endif
   }
 
   // We kill the renderer but don't include a NOTREACHED, because we want the
